### ⚠️ Enumeration side effect, and how it was cleaned up

Probing the group sub-mode needed `--mode "radius-server proxy-server" "group upstream1"`,
and entering that mode **creates** `group upstream1` in the running-config. It is named in
the teardown below and was removed with the rest. A read-only probe of a mode-entering
command is not read-only on this platform; worth knowing before a TRIAGE uses one.

## STEP 3 (designed) -- configure the proxy

### 🔴 FINDING -- `rule N ... server <ip>` cannot reach a server on a non-default port

The obvious configuration was refused:

    awplus(config-radproxy)# server 10.38.22.33 auth-port 11812 acct-port 11813 key testing456
    awplus(config-radproxy)# rule 1 realm example.com server 10.38.22.33
    % Server 10.38.22.33 (1812,1813) is not configured

The `rule ... server <ip>` form resolves the server by **IP plus the DEFAULT ports (1812,1813)**
and offers no way to name the ports, so it can never refer to a server configured on any other
port -- even one that is already in the running-config two lines above. `cfg.py` stopped the
batch at the `% ` line (exit 2), so `proxy enable` was never applied and the bench was never
left half-configured.

**The working form is a server GROUP**, whose own `server <ip> auth-port <n> acct-port <n>`
does take ports:

    awplus(config)# radius-server proxy-server
    awplus(config-radproxy)# group upstream1
    awplus(config-radproxy-group)# server 10.38.22.33 auth-port 11812 acct-port 11813
    awplus(config-radproxy-group)# exit
    awplus(config-radproxy)# rule 1 realm example.com group upstream1
    awplus(config-radproxy)# proxy enable

Applied with `cfg.py`, exit 0, every command echoing a clean prompt (work/cfg-apply2.log).
The full configuration, with the two deliberately different keys:

    radius-server proxy-server
     server 10.38.22.33 auth-port 11812 acct-port 11813 key jQYFBpWNTbzG9aSAztLu6KUBYDCi9VMQVCj2//jSiBg= encrypted
     group upstream1
      server 10.38.22.33 auth-port 11812 acct-port 11813
     nas 10.38.22.33 key h+EeDXRN2hiSvhQ4iErCYKh+SaDpWqcKIQ88roqWCBw= encrypted
     rule 1 realm example.com group upstream1
     proxy enable

(the `nas` key is `testing123`, the `server` key is `testing456`; both are stored and
displayed encrypted only, as in T33407.)

    awplus# show radius proxy-server
                                   Auth  Acct  Auth           Acct
    Server Host/IP Address         Port  Port  Status         Status
    ------------------------------------------------------------------------
    10.38.22.33                    11812 11813 Unknown        Unknown

STEP 3 verdict: PASS. `<dev>.cfg` saved from this configuration: T33409/swi_d.cfg
