VERDICT: PASS -- the x960-56YSQ RADIUS proxy accepted requests from a configured NAS, selected
the upstream group by realm rule, re-originated each request with a new identifier, a
Proxy-State carrying the original id, an added Message-Authenticator and the stripped username,
and relayed the upstream's Accept and Reject back to the NAS. The two legs were proven
cryptographically independent: every NAS-leg reply verifies under `testing123` and none of the
upstream replies do (valid=5/invalid=0 one way, valid=0/invalid=5 the other). `nostrip` changed
the forwarded User-Name and flipped the outcome with nothing else altered, and the whole
configuration was removed with running-config returning byte-identical to its pre-case state.
